.TH PUTS 3
.SH NAME
puts, fputs \- put a string on a stream
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <stdio.h>

int
puts(s)
char *s;

int
fputs(s, stream)
char *s;
FILE *stream;
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B puts
writes the string
.I s
and a newline on
.BR stdout .
.B fputs
writes the string
.I s
on
.IR stream ,
without adding a newline. Neither writes the NUL that ends the string.
.SH "RETURN VALUES"
The last character written (0 for an empty string), or EOF after an
error.
.SH SEE ALSO
gets(3), putc(3), printf(3), ferror(3), stdio(3)
.SH HISTORY
The
.B puts
function first appeared in Version 6 AT&T UNIX, and
.B fputs
in Version 7.
.SH BUGS
.B puts
adds a newline and
.B fputs
does not, in keeping with
.B gets
and
.BR fgets .
